`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
- **Closed enums need a role gate.** F-04-01 is the pattern to watch for in schema contracts: a CHECK constraint on one column is only truthful when another CHECK ties it to the row's role, otherwise every row is forced to assert something false.
- **Route-scoped credentials must be stated per endpoint, not per method.** F-04-02 shows how a single sentence naming only tools/call silently leaves initialize, resources and the GET stream open to the wrong credential kind.
- **"Replaces earlier wording" is a documentation smell.** Appending normative overrides without editing the superseded text (F-04-05) is how canonical documents drift into self-contradiction.
